> is this data stored back in the success reports sheet?

● Looking at the code, yes, the data is stored in sheets, but let me clarify exactly what gets stored where:

  What Gets Stored

  1. Success_Report Sheet (Main Comprehensive Report)

  This sheet stores:
  - Overview statistics (hit rate, profitable rate, avg risk/reward)
  - Top sustained profitable trades (3+ consecutive days)
  - Profitability by holding period (Day 0-5 breakdown)
  - High-impact indicators with correlation values
  - Earnings timing analysis summary
  - Strategy performance breakdown
  - Top 20 winning plays with details
  - Machine learning recommendations

  2. Individual Analysis Sheets (Created by quick reports)

  When you run individual analyses from the menu, they create separate sheets:
  - Top_Winning_Plays - Top 20 trades with indicator snapshots
  - Multi_Day_Analysis - Sustained profitability analysis
  - Indicator_Analysis - Indicator effectiveness correlations
  - Earnings_Timing - Pre/post earnings performance
  - Strategy_Performance - Strategy comparison
  - ML_Export - Machine learning ready CSV data

  Data Storage Format

  The Success_Report sheet is structured with:
  1. Summary sections at the top
  2. Data tables for each analysis type
  3. Conditional formatting to highlight profit/loss values
  4. Auto-resized columns for readability

  Important Note

  The Success Report is read-only analysis - it doesn't write back to your strategy sheets. It:
  - Reads from your strategy sheets (Long Calls, Bull Spreads, etc.)
  - Analyzes the array data in those sheets
  - Creates new report sheets with insights
  - Does NOT modify your original trading data

  Persistence

  - The Success_Report sheet is replaced each time you generate the report
  - Individual analysis sheets are also cleared and regenerated each time
  - To keep historical reports, you could:
    a. Copy the Success_Report sheet with a date stamp
    b. Export to PDF for archival
    c. Create a separate "Report History" sheet

  Accessing the Data

  After running the report:
  1. Look for the Success_Report tab in your spreadsheet
  2. Check individual analysis tabs if you ran specific reports
  3. Use the ML_Export tab for data science work

  The report essentially creates a "snapshot analysis" of your current trading data, helping you identify patterns and optimize        
  your strategy without altering your source data.

